` until the ttl expires.\n  - `getdelSaved` returns `undefined` when nothing was set, then the status once, then `null` afterwards (undefined first, null later).\n\"\"\"\nles=\"\"\"## Lessons for the Atlas\n- editorDataMemory: connection-sample pruning is a no-op (object vs number comparison); memory grows. Fix deliberately during migration, not silently.\n- editorDataMemory: `lockNotification` NaN token makes it non-re-entrant; the interface extraction must decide whether to preserve that.\n- editorDataMemory: `getdelSaved` returns `undefined` then `null`; callers must treat both as falsy.\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(\"## Executor log\\n\",log,1)\ni=s.index(\"## Lessons for the Atlas\")\ns=s[:i]+les\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngit add -A && git commit -qm \"docs(docservice): record editorDataMemory surprising behaviors in PKT-0013\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GfMVS4GJ2FBm26wB5X9Aot\" && git status --short | head"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xbp9WwZp7RYCnPBRdL7yrh","tool_input":{"command":"python3 /tmp/claude-0/-home-claude-euro-office-server-theseus-worktrees-PKT-0013/0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a/scratchpad/rec.py .theseus/queue/in-progress/PKT-0013-*.md && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'E'\ndocs(docservice): record editorDataMemory surprising behaviors in PKT-0013\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GfMVS4GJ2FBm26wB5X9Aot\nE\ngit show --stat HEAD | tail -3"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":13,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I recorded the three surprising behaviors in PKT-0013's Executor log and Lessons for the Atlas, as the rejection asked, and committed it as 737e1b1. The tests and production code are unchanged. Both acceptance commands pass: `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` ran 180 tests with 1 skipped, and eslint is clean on the test file. I ran them before the packet edit, since that edit touched only the packet's markdown.\n\nOne conflict to know about: the run rules say not to edit anything under `.theseus/queue/`, but the rejection said to record these in the packet. I edited only the Executor log and Lessons for the Atlas sections. I didn't touch the packet's state or run any `theseus` command.\n\nThe three behaviors recorded:\n- **Connection-sample pruning:** `setEditorConnections` compares a whole sample object to a number, so nothing is ever pruned and samples grow without bound.\n- **`lockNotification`:** the token is NaN, so the lock isn't re-entrant. The same caller gets `false` until the ttl expires.\n- **`getdelSaved`:** it returns `undefined` when nothing was set, then the status once, then `null`.\n\nThe Lessons entries add that pruning should be fixed deliberately during migration, and that the interface extraction must decide whether to keep the `lockNotification` behavior. They also note that callers must treat both `undefined` and `null` from `getdelSaved` as falsy.","ttft_ms":4276,"type":"result","duration_ms":72317,"uuid":"9b9c2a8b-597f-46c8-b159-e56eff41444c","ttft_stream_ms":3705,"time_to_request_ms":374,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":242,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":18,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":14,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":18,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model